Add mainline support for Xiaomi Mi 8 (dipper) - Qualcomm SDM845.

Imported from the upstream submission by David Heidelberg:

  [PATCH v2 0/2] Introduce support for Xiaomi Mi 8

plus the xbl_mem extension (2 MiB @ 0x85d00000) that Pie-era Xiaomi
firmware requires:

  [PATCH 0/2] arm64: dts: qcom: sdm845-xiaomi: Recent firmware needs bigger XBL

Only the DTS part is imported; the dt-bindings (qcom.yaml) hunk of the
original series is not needed for the build.

Local change (this tree): the upstream revision wires Wi-Fi and Bluetooth
supplies to the internal regulators of a "qcom,wcn3990-pmu" power
sequencer node.  CONFIG_POWER_SEQUENCING_QCOM_WCN in this kernel only
implements the sequencer itself and does not register the node's
"regulators" subnode, so vreg_pmu_* never materialise: ath10k_snoc and
btqca end up with dummy supplies, the sequencer is never triggered and no
wlan0 appears (plus a harmless "qcom-spmi-gpio ... write 0x40 failed" /
pinctrl -EPERM from the now-removed sw_ctrl state).  The wcn3990-pmu node
and sw_ctrl pinctrl state are therefore dropped and &wifi / bluetooth are
fed straight from the PM8998 rails, exactly as beryllium and polaris do.

Local change (this tree): the upstream &sound audio-routing was copied from
beryllium and points "AMIC3" at "MIC BIAS3".  On dipper the built-in mic
capsule is fed from the MIC BIAS1 net instead (as the vendor
dipper-audio-overlay.dtsi also has it), so BIAS3 leaves the capsule unbiased:
the capture path works but is ~35 dB down, which buries speech in noise.
AMIC3 is therefore routed to MIC BIAS1.  (BIAS3 measured ~2 dB of the level,
i.e. negligible, and is dropped entirely.)

